---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Icon from '../components/home/Icon.astro';
import TattooBand from '../components/home/TattooBand.astro';
import '../styles/custom-guides.css';
import NanMadolOperators from '../components/NanMadolOperators.astro';
import { sources } from '../data/nan-madol';

const image = 'https://res.cloudinary.com/doruy2kdr/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,c_fill,g_auto,w_2000,h_900/feature-nan-madol-step-into.jpg';
const contents = [ ['story', 'The story'], ['visiting', 'Plan your visit'], ['prepare', 'What to bring'], ['local-guides', 'Local guides'], ['questions', 'Common questions'] ];
---
<BaseLayout title="Nan Madol Visitor Guide & Local Tours | Pohnpei Island"
  description="Explore Nan Madol’s history, plan a respectful visit, and contact local tour operators. An independent Pohnpei guide with official tourism and UNESCO sources."
  canonical="https://pohnpeiisland.com/nan-madol" image={image}>
  <a href="#guide" class="skip-link">Skip to visitor guide</a>
  <Nav />
  <main id="guide" tabindex="-1" class="custom-guide">
    <section class="custom-guide-hero custom-guide-hero--photo">
      <img src={image} alt="People beside Nan Madol’s basalt walls and waterway" width="2000" height="900" fetchpriority="high" class="custom-guide-hero-image" />
      <div class="custom-guide-hero-shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="custom-guide-hero-inner">
        <p class="custom-guide-kicker">Pohnpei / Culture &amp; history</p>
        <h1 class="custom-guide-heading">Nan Madol</h1>
        <p class="custom-guide-subtitle">A city of stone.<br />A story still living.</p>
        <p class="custom-guide-intro">Meet Pohnpei’s extraordinary lagoon city, understand its significance, and find a local guide to help you visit with care.</p>
        <div class="custom-guide-actions">
          <a href="#visiting" class="guide-button bg-sand text-basalt hover:bg-sand-bright">Plan your visit <Icon name="down" /></a>
          <a href="#local-guides" class="guide-button border border-sand/70 text-sand hover:bg-basalt">Find a local guide <Icon name="down" /></a>
        </div>
        <p class="custom-guide-caption">UNESCO World Heritage Site · Inscribed 2016</p>
      </div>
    <TattooBand class="custom-guide-border-nan-madol" variant="geometric" />
    </section>
    <div class="custom-guide-context px-6 bg-sand-bright border-b border-basalt/15">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto py-5 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-3 md:justify-between text-xs leading-relaxed text-basalt/80">
        <p>An independent Pohnpei guide. <a href={sources.tourism} class="text-link">Visit the official tourism site <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="On this page" class="custom-guide-toc px-6 border-b border-basalt/15">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 py-3">
        {contents.map(([id, label], i) => <a class="min-h-11 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm hover:text-ochre-deep underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href={`#${id}`}><span class="text-ochre-deep text-xs">0{i + 1}</span>{label}</a>)}
      </div>
    </nav>
    <section id="story" class="guide-section bg-sand">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-8 lg:gap-20">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">01 / The story</p><h2 class="section-title">Built in the lagoon.<br /><em>Rooted in Pohnpei.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="guide-prose">
          <p class="font-headline text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug text-basalt">Off Pohnpei’s southeast coast, Nan Madol brings together stone architecture, waterways, and a living cultural inheritance.</p>
          <p>UNESCO describes more than 100 artificial islets, with remains of residences, ceremonial buildings, and tombs. Its English listing dates the surviving structures to 1200–1500 CE and identifies Nan Madol as the Saudeleur dynasty’s ceremonial centre.</p>
          <p>Basalt columns were brought from elsewhere on Pohnpei and arranged in alternating courses. The scale of that work reflects the skill and organisation of its builders. Nan Madol remains connected to Pohnpei’s ceremonial traditions and the Nahnmwarki system of chiefly authority.</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><a href={sources.unesco} class="text-link">Read UNESCO’s account of Nan Madol <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-3xl text-basalt pt-4">What to look for</h3>
          <p>The tourism office highlights the royal mortuary complex, stone courtyards, and tidal canals. A guide can help you understand what you’re seeing and explain local traditions. Ask which areas are appropriate to enter before exploring.</p>
          <p>JADESA’s route description calls the mortuary destination Nan Douwas. Its boat itinerary passes several islets before reaching it. <a href="https://myjadesa.com/pages/tours" class="text-link">See JADESA’s route description <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
          <aside class="border-l-2 border-ochre-deep pl-6 py-2">
            <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl text-basalt mb-3">A place to care for</h3>
            <p>UNESCO inscribed Nan Madol in 2016 and currently lists it as World Heritage in Danger. It identifies silting waterways and mangrove growth among the threats to its structures. <a href={sources.unesco} class="text-link">Read the conservation context <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="visiting" class="guide-section bg-sand-bright">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Plan your visit</p>
        <h2 class="section-title max-w-2xl mb-6">Start with the route.<br /><em>Let the tide set the time.</em></h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-basalt/80 mb-10">The tourism office places access at Temwen Island and recommends a local guide. For the walking approach, it describes rough road sections and a tidal-flat crossing, with mid to low tide easier for access. <a href={sources.tourism} class="text-link">Official visiting guidance <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <article class="bg-sand-bright border border-basalt/15 p-6 md:p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Road + walking</p><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Arrange the whole journey.</h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed text-basalt/80">Ask your guide or accommodation to confirm pickup, the road approach, walking conditions, and the return trip. Tell them where you’re staying. Confirm the day’s crossing conditions before setting out; a general tide recommendation cannot tell you whether a crossing is suitable for you.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="bg-sand-bright border border-basalt/15 p-6 md:p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Boat or kayak</p><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">See the waterways with a guide.</h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed text-basalt/80">JADESA advertises guided boat and kayak visits; its Nan Madol boat trips depend on the tide. Ask about departure location, boarding, equipment, and the route for your date. Other listed operators can explain their own arrangements. <a href="#local-guides" class="text-link">Compare local contacts <Icon name="down" /></a></p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 bg-basalt text-sand p-6 md:p-10 grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.5fr] gap-6">
          <div><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-3">Before you agree to a trip</h3><p class="text-sm text-sand/85 leading-relaxed">Get a current quote and a clear plan directly from your operator.</p></div>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-sand/90">
            <li>What is the total cost, including transport, guiding, and any access fees? How should you pay?</li>
            <li>Where will you meet, how long is the outing, and is your return transport included?</li>
            <li>How much walking, wading, or boarding is involved? Mention mobility needs and children’s ages.</li>
            <li>What happens if weather or tide conditions change? Confirm cancellation terms.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="prepare" class="guide-section bg-sand">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / Prepare</p><h2 class="section-title mb-6">Pack for <em>water and weather.</em></h2>
          <p class="text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">Use this as a starting checklist and ask your guide what your particular route requires.</p>
          <ul class="divide-y divide-basalt/15 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="py-4"><strong>Secure footwear with grip.</strong> Ask what works for the walking and water conditions.</li>
            <li class="py-4"><strong>Water, sun protection, and rain cover.</strong> Pack what you’ll need for the outing.</li>
            <li class="py-4"><strong>A waterproof bag.</strong> Keep your phone, camera, and valuables protected.</li>
            <li class="py-4"><strong>Insect repellent and a change of clothes.</strong> Prepare for time outdoors and the possibility of getting wet.</li>
            <li class="py-4"><strong>The agreed payment.</strong> Confirm payment method and access fees in advance.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="md:pt-12">
          <h2 class="section-title mb-6">Visit with <em>respect.</em></h2>
          <p class="text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">The tourism office describes Nan Madol as a sacred place. Let local guidance shape your visit.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-4 text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed">
            <li>Ask permission before entering areas beyond your agreed route or photographing people and ceremonies.</li>
            <li>Leave stones, coral, and other objects where they are. Avoid climbing or disturbing the structures.</li>
            <li>Give burial places space and follow your guide’s instructions about appropriate conduct.</li>
            <li>Take rubbish away with you. Leave room for others to experience the site quietly.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-8 font-headline text-2xl italic text-ochre-deep">Bring your curiosity.<br />Make time to listen.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <NanMadolOperators />
    <section id="questions" class="guide-section bg-sand-bright">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 / Common questions</p><h2 class="section-title mb-8">A few things <em>to know.</em></h2>
        <div class="divide-y divide-basalt/20 border-y border-basalt/20">
          <details class="py-5"><summary>How much does a visit cost?</summary><p>Request a quote for your date, group size, and route. Check whether it includes transfers, guiding, equipment, and access fees. We don’t publish a universal price because these arrangements need to be confirmed with the provider.</p></details>
          <details class="py-5"><summary>Can I visit without a guide?</summary><p>The tourism office recommends a guide for historical and cultural context. If you plan to travel independently, ask the tourism office about current access and local arrangements first. A map alone won’t explain permission, crossing conditions, or the significance of the places you enter.</p></details>
          <details class="py-5"><summary>Is the visit suitable for children or limited mobility?</summary><p>Discuss your group’s needs before agreeing to a trip. Ask for specifics about uneven ground, water crossings, steps, boat boarding, seating, and assistance. We have not verified an accessible route; a boat trip should not be assumed to remove those barriers.</p></details>
          <details class="py-5"><summary>Can I combine Nan Madol with another stop?</summary><p>Ask your operator to suggest a realistic itinerary, allowing time for transport and the tide. The tourism office describes visits that can include waterfalls or village sightseeing. Agree on each stop and its access arrangements rather than assuming extras are included.</p></details>
          <details class="py-5"><summary>Does this website take bookings?</summary><p>No. Contact details connect you directly with the business. Confirm availability, price, and terms with the operator before making your arrangements. For wider assistance, <a href={sources.contact} class="text-link">contact the Pohnpei Tourism Office</a>.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="sources" class="guide-section bg-sand">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h2 class="section-title mb-5">Make your <em>next connection.</em></h2><p class="text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">Have dates in mind? Compare places to stay, then share your accommodation’s location with a local operator to arrange your visit.</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href="/places-to-stay" class="guide-button bg-lagoon text-white hover:bg-basalt">Find a place to stay <Icon name="arrow" /></a><a href="#local-guides" class="guide-button border border-basalt/30 hover:bg-sand-bright">Find a local guide <Icon name="up" /></a></div></div>
        <div class="text-sm text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed">
          <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl text-basalt mb-4">About this guide &amp; our sources</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">PohnpeiIsland.com is an independent guide with no formal tourism-office affiliation. We write our own visitor guidance using the sources below. Source review is not an on-site inspection or a confirmation of business availability.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li><a class="text-link" href={sources.unesco}>UNESCO: history, significance, and conservation <Icon name="arrow" /></a></li>
            <li><a class="text-link" href={sources.tourism}>Pohnpei Tourism Office: visiting Nan Madol <Icon name="arrow" /></a></li>
            <li><a class="text-link" href={sources.operators}>Pohnpei Tourism Office: full operator directory <Icon name="arrow" /></a></li>
            <li><a class="text-link" href="https://myjadesa.com/pages/tours">JADESA: routes and tour information <Icon name="arrow" /></a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-5">Business-specific sources appear with each listing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
